 "comments": [
  {
   "address": 1024,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "bit 7 set by the play interrupt once per screen swap ($0913); the main loop at $0E5F waits for it and clears it"
  },
  {
   "address": 1025,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the joystick byte read from $DC00 by $0B3C, shifted out bit by bit into $0402-$0406"
  },
  {
   "address": 1026,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "five flags, $80 when pressed: up, down, left, right, fire (from $DC00 bits 0-4, by $0B3C)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1031,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "first sprite row's Y for the terrain sprites: the scroll's coarse row offset plus $48 ($0B7B), set by $0CDF"
  },
  {
   "address": 1032,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "how far the eight terrain sprites' X positions are rotated through $0413-$041A ($0BB4), set by $0CDF"
  },
  {
   "address": 1033,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "terrain sprite multicolour 0, from the level header's colour table at $E060 ($0E1C)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1034,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "terrain sprites' own colour, from $E064 ($0E1C)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1035,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "terrain sprite multicolour 1, from $E068 ($0E1C)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1036,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the view's horizontal position in pixels within a column (0-7); with $040D it says which part of the level is shown"
  },
  {
   "address": 1037,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the view's horizontal position in columns"
  },
  {
   "address": 1038,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "where the view should move to, fine part; set by the cursor at the screen edge"
  },
  {
   "address": 1039,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "where the view should move to, column part"
  },
  {
   "address": 1040,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "this pass's scroll step, fine part, at most one column ($0DDB)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1041,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "this pass's scroll step, columns (0 or 1)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1043,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the eight terrain sprites' X positions, 24 pixels apart, rotated into $D000-$D00E by $0B73"
  },
  {
   "address": 1051,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the X positions' ninth bits, built for $D010 by $0B73"
  },
  {
   "address": 1052,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "counts frames since the last screen swap ($08EF)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1053,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 when the main loop has drawn the hidden screen and it may be shown ($0E74)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1055,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "set to 6 by $0C90"
  },
  {
   "address": 1057,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "which of the two screens is shown: 0 for $4000, 1 for $4400; toggled by the interrupt at each swap ($0904)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1400,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the release rate as a step 0-23 ($0B14 down to the level's minimum at $E03C, $0B30 up to 23)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1403,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "set to $80 by every play interrupt ($08EA); $0DF5 waits on it to count frames"
  },
  {
   "address": 1407,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 when the keyboard scan at $0A5A found a key down"
  },
  {
   "address": 1408,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 after a press of DEL (key 11 of the scan table, $0AE7); cleared when $DC01 reads a key at the start of the scan; with $0581 and $0582 it detects DEL pressed twice"
  },
  {
   "address": 1409,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "counts passes with no key down since DEL was pressed ($0AA6); a second DEL within 8 of them arms the nuke"
  },
  {
   "address": 1410,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 on a pass with no key down after DEL ($0AA9), so that holding DEL does not count as two presses"
  },
  {
   "address": 1411,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 once DEL has been pressed twice within 8 key-free passes ($0ADC)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1413,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "counts passes between steps of the release rate while + or - is held (one step every 7)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1414,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 while SHIFT is held (key 10 of the scan table; SHIFT LOCK holds it down), cleared at the start of every scan ($0A70): the game is paused"
  },
  {
   "address": 1415,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "counts 30 passes down once no lemming is left in play; at 0 the level ends ($0F31)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1416,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 once the level has ended: by time, by the back-arrow key while paused, or with every lemming gone ($0F36, $0ECA)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1460,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the scroll column whose terrain characters $0D1F last copied"
  },
  {
   "address": 1461,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the scroll position, fine, at the last frame ($0CFF)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1462,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the scroll position, columns, at the last frame ($0CF9)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1463,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "lemmings released so far; when it reaches the level's count at $E039, no more come"
  },
  {
   "address": 1472,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the skill chosen with keys 1-8 (0-7), set by $0AB4; also moves the panel's highlight sprite ($0A4A)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1474,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the play area's background colour, from the level header at $E05C ($0E1C)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1756,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "the pause flag copied at the start of the pass ($0E3C): when set, the clock ($0EE9) and $1DD9 are skipped ($0E4E)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1757,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 from the moment the level ends; stops the play interrupt calling $1916 ($091E)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1758,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "$80 once the clock has run out ($0EC7)"
  },
  {
   "address": 1759,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "counts frames in fives up to 50: one second of the clock at $0EE9"
  },
  {
   "address": 52256,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "jump table of the resident loader (nine JMPs)"
  },
  {
   "address": 52283,
   "type": "line",
   "text": "reads an eight-byte header at $9000 into zero page $02-$0D"
  },
  {
   "address": 52622,
